  <reporting-org ref="US-GOV-9" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Department of the Interior</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CONSERVATION OF THREE CRITICAL WETLANDS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will: 1.a.) Establish 10-year (or longer) land conservation agreements on 821 hectares/2,028 acres. 1.b.) Expand a Ramsar site by adding 2,500 hectares/6,175 acres to the current 17,000 hectares/42,008 acres already decreed. 2) Increase water infiltration with soil restoration techniques on (1,396 hectares/3,449 acres) of the newly protected areas, through building soil borders, keyline treatment, filtering dams, and stone barriers and through reforestation; of these (3,449 acres), (701 hectares/1,731 acres) will be enhanced and (1,255 hectares/3,099 acres) will be restored. 3) Reduce sewage contamination in Santiaguillo by building biofilters and biodigesters. 4) Develop the XXI Wetlands Training Course in Durango. 5) Conduct environmental education campaigns in the Santiaguillo and Bustillos watersheds and celebrate World Migratory Bird Day. 6) Develop a restoration strategy for Laguna de Bustillos. 7) Build the capacity of local landowners in Laguna de Bustillos to monitor social and environmental variables and implement restoration and ecotechnologies in Laguna de Bustillos. 8) Survey waterfowl in Can de Fernndez. 9) Determine the bioaccumulation of pollutants in waterfowl and pollutant sources in Santiaguillo</narrative>
  </description>
